











-- PURPOSE-DRIVEN SCHEMAS (GH #862, and the structural cause of #860).
--
-- Everything installed into one flat `laplace` namespace. That is not cosmetic: it
-- is the reason 232 of 351 function bodies carry `SET search_path`. With a single
-- namespace an unqualified reference APPEARS to work, so nobody qualified anything,
-- and each body then needed the clause to resolve at runtime -- which costs the
-- planner SQL inlining and, in a WHERE or ORDER BY, the index path (#860, measured:
-- a SET-carrying function plans as one opaque `Function Scan`, its clause-free
-- sibling inlines to an Index Scan). The clause was never security: zero of the 232
-- are SECURITY DEFINER.
--
-- With purpose schemas a cross-family call MUST qualify, because no search_path
-- brings a sibling schema into scope. Correctness becomes structural instead of 232
-- copies of a clause, and `consensus.eff_mu(...)` says where the thing lives instead
-- of `laplace.` deferring the question to install time.
--
-- The names come from the directory layout, which already encodes the intent, and
-- from spec 37's opcode families:
--
--   consensus   the fold and its edge reads          (WEIGHT, SCAN)
--   converse    the speaking loop                    (SEQUENCE)
--   lexical     words, senses, definitions           (SENSE, RESOLVE)
--   taxonomy    hierarchy traversal                  (TRAVERSE)
--   generation  synthesis and the forward pass       (ELECT)
--   structural  geometry, coordinates, trajectories
--   chess       the chess modality
--   realize     rendering and readback               (REALIZE)
--   ops         diagnostics, census, health          (WITNESS)
--
-- WHY THIS IS SAFE TO ADD BEFORE ANY FUNCTION MOVES: creating the schemas changes
-- nothing about where existing objects live. `laplace` stays the extension's own
-- schema and keeps every object it has; these are empty namespaces that families
-- migrate into one at a time, each migration a self-contained change that can be
-- verified on its own. The alternative -- moving 351 files in one commit -- is
-- unreviewable and unbisectable.
--
-- MIGRATION STATUS (2026-08-07): purpose families migrated (converse/lexical/
-- taxonomy/realize/consensus/generation/structural/chess/ops census). Identity/μ/
-- relation/readback/inspect/highway-index and remaining ops helpers still move.
-- Hot tables stay in the extension schema until a table cut. api() lists all
-- purpose schemas. Highway mask bits stay in the extension schema (index deps).
--
-- Every purpose schema belongs to laplace_substrate. Usually CREATE records that
-- membership automatically. `ops` predates the split on populated hosts, though:
-- DbUp created it for the file-backed diagnostics before this extension version
-- existed. PostgreSQL rejects CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS from an extension script
-- when the conflicting schema is not already an extension member. Create only
-- absent namespaces, then absorb any legacy namespace into the extension. This is
-- the versioned upgrade path -- no deploy-time ALTER and no permanently shared
-- ownership exception.
--
-- They are NOT added to any search_path: that omission is the entire point.
DO $purpose_schemas$
DECLARE
    s text;
BEGIN
    FOREACH s IN ARRAY ARRAY['consensus','converse','lexical','taxonomy',
                             'generation','structural','chess','realize','ops']
    LOOP
        IF to_regnamespace(s) IS NULL THEN
            EXECUTE format('CREATE SCHEMA %I', s);
        ELSIF NOT EXISTS (
            SELECT 1
            FROM pg_catalog.pg_depend d
            JOIN pg_catalog.pg_extension e ON e.oid = d.refobjid
            WHERE d.classid = 'pg_catalog.pg_namespace'::regclass
              AND d.objid = to_regnamespace(s)
              AND d.refclassid = 'pg_catalog.pg_extension'::regclass
              AND d.deptype = 'e'
              AND e.extname = 'laplace_substrate'
        ) THEN
            EXECUTE format('ALTER EXTENSION laplace_substrate ADD SCHEMA %I', s);
        END IF;
    END LOOP;
END
$purpose_schemas$;

COMMENT ON SCHEMA consensus  IS 'Laplace: the fold and its edge reads (spec 37 WEIGHT, SCAN).';
COMMENT ON SCHEMA converse   IS 'Laplace: the speaking loop (spec 37 SEQUENCE).';
COMMENT ON SCHEMA lexical    IS 'Laplace: words, senses, definitions (spec 37 SENSE, RESOLVE).';
COMMENT ON SCHEMA taxonomy   IS 'Laplace: hierarchy traversal (spec 37 TRAVERSE).';
COMMENT ON SCHEMA generation IS 'Laplace: synthesis and the forward pass (spec 37 ELECT).';
COMMENT ON SCHEMA structural IS 'Laplace: geometry, coordinates, trajectories.';
COMMENT ON SCHEMA chess      IS 'Laplace: the chess modality.';
COMMENT ON SCHEMA realize    IS 'Laplace: rendering and readback (spec 37 REALIZE).';
COMMENT ON SCHEMA ops        IS 'Laplace: diagnostics, census, health (spec 37 WITNESS).';

-- Same grants the extension schema carries. A reader that can call laplace.* can
-- call these; the split is about structure and planning, never about privilege.
DO $purpose$
DECLARE
    s text;
BEGIN
    FOREACH s IN ARRAY ARRAY['consensus','converse','lexical','taxonomy',
                             'generation','structural','chess','realize','ops']
    LOOP
        EXECUTE format('GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA %I TO PUBLIC', s);
    END LOOP;
END
$purpose$;
-- PURPOSE-SCHEMA RELOCATION — UPGRADE PATH ONLY (GH #862).
--
-- This file is listed in manifest.upgrade and NOT in manifest.install, for the
-- same reason indexes/drop_entities_tier_btree.sql.in is: a fresh database has
-- nothing to relocate. Every function below is created directly at its purpose
-- address by the install script, so on CREATE EXTENSION this work does not
-- exist. It exists only to carry an ALREADY-INSTALLED substrate forward.
--
-- WHY ALTER ... SET SCHEMA AND NOT DROP + CREATE.
--
-- PostgreSQL records dependencies by OID. A view, an index expression, an ACL,
-- a COMMENT, and another function's stored parse tree all reference a function
-- through pg_proc.oid, never through its name. ALTER FUNCTION ... SET SCHEMA is
-- a catalog update: the row keeps its OID, so every one of those dependents
-- follows the move silently and nothing has to be rebuilt.
--
-- DROP FUNCTION laplace.f + CREATE FUNCTION purpose.f mints a NEW oid. Every
-- dependent then either blocks the drop (RESTRICT, the default -- this is the
-- 2BP01 that entities_highway_bits_gin raised against
-- laplace.laplace_highway_mask_bits) or is destroyed by CASCADE. Compatibility
-- wrappers patch that symptom while permanently doubling the API surface, which
-- is the exact condition #862 exists to remove. So: relocate, never re-create.
--
-- IDEMPOTENT BY CONSTRUCTION, NOT BY DEMOLITION. The loop reads what is
-- actually in pg_proc. On a second run the source schema no longer holds the
-- function, the cursor yields nothing, and the block is a no-op. Overloads are
-- handled because pg_get_function_identity_arguments enumerates each signature
-- separately. Nothing is dropped, so re-running can never lose a dependent.
--
-- ORDERING: this must run BEFORE the function definition files in
-- manifest.upgrade. It moves the old body to the new address; the definition
-- files that follow then CREATE OR REPLACE that same address, which updates the
-- body in place and again preserves the OID.
DO $relocate$
DECLARE
    m record;
    r record;
BEGIN
    FOR m IN
        SELECT * FROM (VALUES
            ('_realize_canonical', 'realize', '_canonical'),
            ('_realize_defines', 'realize', '_defines'),
            ('_realize_has_name', 'realize', '_has_name'),
